before the video begins I'd like to  thank you all for two years of anime  culture Corner every comment like and  frankly every extra minute spent  watching my videos means the world to me  and I couldn't do this all without you  guys I know I don't upload as much as I  used to not only is life getting busy  but I've gotten to the point where I  genuinely value quality over quantity of  my videos even if it means that you know  the views kind of suffer I I hope you  guys see this reflected in my uploads I  started off with nothing on this channel  and we've managed to come farther than I  ever could have imagined so I look  forward to many more years to come  whether you're New or Old to the channel  I'm glad you're here let's start the  video  foreign  there's something about a broken  character that speaks to us  Humanity's best attempts to relate to  literature throughout history from the  animals of Shakespeare all the way to  the bound tomes of Berserk it always  feels like the factor that ties us  together most of all is tragedy  not just any sad story the dark  backstory of an irrelevant side  character no matter how deep won't tug  on our heartstrings the same way that it  might on someone we know well implying  that our strong connection to Broken  characters isn't as simple as being just  a figment of our Collective empathy but  also includes even stronger factors like  our devotion and dedication to the  well-written character  on top of this there are innumerable  masterful stories Without Tragedy with  Incredible main characters who haven't  experienced any kind of immense sadness  that would warrant being quote unquote  broken  but I personally feel like many of the  works of fiction Manga and Anime  specifically that create a character who  I share a very strong bond with and love  so dearly all push their protagonists to  their mental and emotional limits at one  point or another  crushing their hopes destroying their  dreams and leaving them to suffer the  horrors of Life a breaking point if you  will  and so it does beg the very important  question why does breaking our  protagonists make them so beautiful  who do you think of when I say a broken  character from manga or anime guts  dorphin Aaron even all valid answers and  let me try to describe what I think  encompasses being broken before  continuing on  there are many different ways to Define  it and I don't think mine is absolutely  correct not at all but when looking at  the long list of characters like this  when I created this the common thread I  always seem to find is the lonely  struggle  not only are these characters scarred by  a certain tragedy due to external  factors or because of something they  themselves did whether it was at the  beginning of the story or something they  are forced to deal with throughout it  they also find that on their path to  Redemption that ensues they are always  utterly alone  sometimes they have people around them  still sometimes they don't but no one  ever truly understands them regardless  well no one except us  manga readers will see these characters  feelings of being misunderstood and then  attempt to relate their struggles as a  sigma male to gutses saying he's just  like me for real when they most  certainly have not had everyone they've  known and loved be brutally massacred  and or violated by their best friend who  uses them all as sacrifices in the  pursuit of godhood  but in all seriousness I think this is  an important point to make because it is  not the struggle itself that makes these  characters relatable really it's how  they cope with it and their struggle  later to express their pain emotionally  No One Alive can really understand okabe  from Stein's gate who faces the  consequences of his unchecked pursuit of  time travel a power no man should bear  the burden of possessing what allows us  to sympathize and understand him is his  inability to divulge onto others the  pain he is going through as he is forced  to travel through time for the greater  good  okabe's is a unique struggle because he  is the sole character in the world of  Steins Gate who actually can understand  across timelines just about everyone  physically wouldn't be able to  understand even if they tried  but the same Trend regardless still  follows all of our broken characters  guts is the only one who knows what the  eclipse was who Griffith really is and  the meaning behind his brand of  sacrifice  even after he's gained a new comrades  new people to love they don't really  know guts  few remember the person thorphin used to  be and those who do characters who've  been born into the Viking and Norse  climate can't understand why thorfin  wishes to repent for a life of battle he  should be proud of  why he wouldn't want to die in Valhalla  with the rest of them  these three are some of the most beloved  characters out there  so why does this shared feeling of being  misunderstood connect to us so much what  is the appeal  well there is something intrinsically  human about keeping your emotions hidden  Society shuns emotions in a way the  overtly masculine and rugged worlds of  both berserk and Finland Saga are  perfect examples of this  but some of it also does stem from our  natural desire to better ourselves and  overcome feelings on our own  a feeling of Independence and  self-imposed strength  the contrast between this internal  battle and the character's exterior adds  that depth to them  contributing to the lonely struggle  looking past the robust bravery one  needs to charge into battle or the  endurance to harden your body into an  indestructible shell hiding emotions is  something that everyone can understand  and connect to the loneliness it brings  even the strongest people people like  guts endorphin characters who are  written to exemplify that bravery and  endurance feel those same emotions and  the struggle to admit them  in a way broken characters like this  speak to us so much more because the  more broken one is the more human they  are  the more they are forced to confront the  sad truths of human society how it's  chewed them up and churned them out  forcing them to suffer though he might  not be able to feel the extent of the  tragedy itself really understand the  pain of the eclipse it is the lonely  path the characters take afterwards that  we all can share in everyone feels these  emotions of sadness tragedy that are  rooted in a basic human function so  common that even your everyday manga  reader or Anime Watcher can feel some  kind of connection  an appeal to our Humanity a broken  character isn't just one whose mind  breaks and emotions collapse and are  forced to confront the Terrors of the  world but one who also breaks the  constraints of fiction and becomes a  real genuine person in front of our eyes  we can learn how even after facing such  tragedy they can still make something of  it made up characters become a real life  source of Hope  that's pretty beautiful to me  music on today's video is all courtesy  of eachon an incredible musician and  close friend of mine check out his work  on all streaming platforms the links in  the bio  as always this has been the anime  culture corner I hope you enjoyed the  video don't forget to like And subscribe  for future in-depth show manga and  character analyzes and thanks for two  years  foreign  [Music]
 

